PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — IntersectImplicit passes MILLIMETRES into an
int narrow-band parameter (ledger row U1; PicoPie Fix 2 reached the same
diagnosis independently).

`Voxels oVox(oVoxelSize(), fBackgroundMM())` sends the background distance in
world units (mm) into the constructor's `int nNarrowBand`. The implicit
float->int truncation narrows the fresh grid's band: 3 at 1.0 mm voxels by
coincidence, 1 at 0.4-0.7 mm, and 0 below ~1/3 mm — where
FloatGrid::create(0) yields a zero-background "level set" and the call THROWS.
The intended value is simply the member the class already holds:
m_nSdfNarrowBand. One line.

Verification shape (picovoxel SKv2-0 V0.10): at 1.0 mm the fixed and original
paths are value-identical (the truncation lands on 3 there); at 0.25 mm the
original throws while the fix matches a reference construction built from
never-truncated paths, classification-identical with identical meshes.

PROPOSAL, NOT APPLIED LOCALLY: picovoxel ships the fix as sibling-TU exports
(Voxels_IntersectImplicit{,Tape}Fast) so the vendored tree stays pristine and
the original remains the differential oracle.

--- a/Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h
+++ b/Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h
@@ -387,7 +387,7 @@
     {
         PKTRACE(Voxels_IntersectImplicit);
         
-        Voxels oVox(oVoxelSize(), fBackgroundMM());
+        Voxels oVox(oVoxelSize(), m_nSdfNarrowBand);
         
         CoordBBox oBBox = m_roGrid->evalActiveVoxelBoundingBox();
         
